        ⛔ THE ELEVENTH ROW. /etc/services is host data glibc reads, does
           not carry, and none of the ten covers. NSS is closed for
           DISPATCH — __nss_configure_lookup pins the services database to
           `files` — and `files` still means /etc/services, which 3 of
           11 environments do not have.
        ⚠ AND IT IS NOT A MUSL STORY, it is the reverse: all four musl
           environments SHIP the file and 3 glibc ones do not.
        ⚠ The failure is a NULL return rather than a wrong number, so it is
           louder than gconv's and timezone's. A caller that checks the
           return value sees it; one that does not dereferences NULL.
  ok    vanilla static rows that CRASHED outright      = 1
        crashed: archlinux-latest(exit 136)
        ⛔ exit 136 = 128 + 8 = SIGFPE, and the last answer printed is
           `shells=ok`, so the call that dies is gethostid().
        ⭐ gethostid() with no /etc/hostid (0 of 11 have one) resolves the
           machine's own hostname — an NSS `hosts` lookup. On Arch that
           dlopens libnss_mymachines and a second libc enters the process.
        ⚠ THIS IS ROW 1 (NSS), NOT A NEW ROW. What is new is the REACH:
           gethostid() had never been probed here. experiments/63- measures
           whether __nss_configure_lookup covers it.

